  "reference": "Excel 16.115 for macOS. Two independently saved workbooks with 926 scalar observations of positions in the four result arrays. Four additional dynamic arrays were entered directly in Excel (38 cells). With intercept, without intercept, omitted predictors, tall and wide layouts, repeated, zero, shifted, nearly collinear, exact and log-domain cases. A1 changes from 7 to 12.",
  "implementation": "Column-pivoted Householder QR on the design matrix, withholding the covariance calculations when statistics are not requested. Predictions retain centered coordinates. Pre-existing input limits of 255 regressors and one billion row × predictor-squared operations remain.",
  "thresholds": "Types and errors match exactly. General relative/absolute bounds are 2e-10/1e-12. For the named near-collinear input the statistic bounds are 4e-9 and the intercept standard error reference bound is 2e-6; all of those candidate statistics must separately match an independent 75-digit solution within 4e-9. Large-offset predictions must be within one Excel-scale ULP and separately within 2e-12 of the 75-digit solution. The exactly linear input has zero true residual and unbounded F; both programs give finite F > 1 / epsilon², with different roundoff in the residual. All raw strict deviations are listed per platform.",
